                        <p>
                            To this day, Texas still has 3 dry counties in the state. Hays County, which borders the
                            Austin,
                            Texas,
                            area
                            was
                            also a dry county until fairly recently in the grand scheme of time. During the early years
                            of
                            being
                            a
                            wet
                            county, Dripping Springs was considered a small town, with not much in the way of
                            entertainment.
                            By
                            2018
                            the
                            landscape had completed shifted. Huge destination breweries and distilleries could now be
                            found
                            through
                            out
                            the
                            Texas Hill Country.
                            <br><br>
                            Before Acopon Brewing Co. was born, John McIntosh and Dave Niemeyer,opened the first craft
                            beer
                            bar
                            in
                            Dripping Springs right on historic Mercer St. When they approached me to help them develop
                            an
                            identity
                            for
                            their new brewery, we knew we needed to do somthing a bit more unexpected.
                            <br><br>
                            I first tasked them to develop a unique name with meaning, and flexibility for theming. The
                            unfortunate
                            common
                            cliche for most breweries is to name it after their local area; their city, local landmark,
                            local river, or
                            something
                            to do
                            with local history. This makes sense from a community perspective, you want to push your
                            locality,
                            but
                            is
                            also
                            fairly boring. I instead tasked them with focusing more on what actually makes them unique
                            which
                            was
                            their
                            main
                            beer styles; traditional English Ales served from a hand pump.
                            <br><br>
                            <strong>Acopon (<i>ak’-o-pon</i>)</strong> is an obsolete English word that originated in
                            the
                            16th
                            century, primarily
                            referring
                            to a
                            health tonic, cordial, or restorative medicine.
                            <br><br>
                            With the name chosen, I explored a variety of ideas primarily dealing with health/healing
                            including
                            alchemy,
                            potions, and tonics; in the end however, we decided on a Plague Doctor. In the times of the
                            bubonic
                            plague,
                            most
                            plague doctors were simply public servants and not doctors at all. In that sense, a pint
                            beer
                            may
                            restore
                            your
                            spirit, though it's not advocated to actually be healthy for you, especially in excess.
                            <br><br>
                            The theming has continued over the years not only with traditional English beer names such
                            as
                            “*Gas
                            Pipes”*,
                            named after the street lamps of London before they were electric powered, but also for other
                            European
                            folklore
                            such as “*Hans Trapp”*, the Bavarian version of Krampus, and “*Polednice”*, a noon demon in
                            Slavic
                            mythology.
                            Sticking to these themes not only makes for a more memorable brand, but creates a ton of
                            merchandising
                            opportunities, which not only boosts the breweries brand awareness in the public, but is a
                            major
                            revenue
                            driver
                            for small brewpubs.
